{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01HQF8MQ5hfwx6aaAjVBioTM","type":"tool_result","content":"---\nrole: lead\nstatus: done\nattempt: 1\nnext: [triage:engineer]\nworker: engineer\n---\nThis issue adds an optional `fetched:` list to worker role files. Close-out parses it strictly, and the worker PR body renders it as a Fetched inputs list. The issue also brings docs/proposal.md's egress and network text in line with the code. The dependency (part 1, the per-role network setting) has already landed, so the work can start, and engineer is the only triage planner and worker in this repository.\n\n## Routing\n- triage:engineer: steps for parsing and validating `fetched:` in internal/closeout and carrying it on the worker result, rendering the PR body in internal/worker/pr.go, and editing the proposal. Includes table tests for each invalid field and PR-body tests with and without entries.\n- worker engineer: Go change with unit tests plus the docs/proposal.md edits.\n\n## Open issues\n- The change adds to the `.ard/` file contract and touches several places (closeout, worker, docs). No architect or documentation-planner role exists, so the triage engineer should cover the contract wording in the proposal as well.\n- The proposal must describe egress \"as the code does\". The engineer should check which enforcement parts of the tracking issue have landed, so the docs describe what exists today and not what is planned.\n- The issue mentions a per-fixture CAPTURE.md convention. The plan should say whether this change adds or updates any CAPTURE.md file, or only documents the convention.\n# ard configuration for albertcbrown/ard (dogfooding). Started from `ard init`'s\n# template; human-owned. ard serve reads it from origin/main.\n# Anything unset takes its built-in default (docs/proposal.md, Configuration).\n# Validate with `ard config check`. ard serve reads this file from origin/main.\n\n# label: only issues a maintainer labels for triage enter the pipeline.\n# all: every human-filed issue enters.\nintake: { mode: label }\n\nmerge:\n  # A PR touching any of these waits for a human approval. There is no\n  # built-in list: removing an entry removes its gate. An entry ending in /\n  # is a directory prefix; anything else is a glob (quote globs starting with *).\n  protected_paths:\n    - .github/\n    - .ard/config.yaml\n    - .ard/scanners/\n    - .ard/triage/\n    - .ard/workers/\n    - .ard/reviewers/\n    - \"**/CODEOWNERS\"\n    # Agent instructions a PR could plant to steer later agents.\n    - CLAUDE.md\n    - \"**/CLAUDE.md\"\n    - AGENTS.md\n    - \"**/AGENTS.md\"\n    - .claude/\n    - .mcp.json\n    # What builds, signs and deploys ard itself (docs/proposal.md, Delivery).\n    - \"Jenkinsfile*\"\n    - Dockerfile\n    - .dockerignore\n    - deploy/\n\noverrides:\n  scanners/cve: { every: 6h, max_open: 10, group_size: 1, autoclose: true }\n  # Phase 1 agent roles (the ard init starter set, #39 Gate 2).\n  triage/lead:  { model: claude-opus-5-5, timeout: 15m }\n  triage/engineer: { model: claude-sonnet-5-5 }\n  workers/engineer: { model: claude-sonnet-5-5, timeout: 60m, tests: make test }\n  reviewers/eng-review: { model: claude-sonnet-5-5 }\ninternal/closeout:\nallow.go\nallow_test.go\ncause_test.go\ncloseout.go\ncloser_test.go\ncomment.go\ncomment_test.go\ncommit.go\ndoc.go\nenv_test.go\nfacts.go\nleadworker_test.go\nnext.go\npaths.go\npaths_test.go\nplan.go\nplan_merge.go\nplan_merge_test.go\nplan_test.go\nprepare.go\nprepare_allow_test.go\nprepare_test.go\nprgone_test.go\nreview.go\nreview_test.go\nrolefile.go\nrolefile_test.go\ntestdata\nusage.go\nusage_test.go\nworker.go\nworker_test.go\n\ninternal/worker:\nbranch.go\ncandidates.go\ncandidates_test.go\ndoc.go\nfacts.go\nfeedback.go\nguard.go\nharness_test.go\nloop.go\nloop_test.go\npr.go\nrun.go\ntype.go\nunit_test.go\n.ard/276:\ncosts\nlogs\ntriage-engineer.md\ntriage-lead.md\n\n.ard/297:\ncosts\nlogs\nplan.md\nreview-eng-review.md\ntriage-engineer.md\ntriage-lead.md\nworker-engineer.md\ninternal/closeout/closeout.go:724:// postReview posts a review job's summary and findings once: one PR review\ninternal/closeout/prepare.go:129:\t\tfindings   []Finding // of the redacted role file\ninternal/closeout/prepare.go:150:\t\t\t\t\thit += \" (rules: \" + ruleList(res.Findings) + \")\"\ninternal/closeout/prepare.go:156:\t\t\t\t\tsummary, findings = crf.Summary, crf.Findings\ninternal/closeout/prepare.go:232:\t\tplan = needsHumanPlan(j, rf.Status, \"findings unreadable after redaction\")\ninternal/closeout/prepare.go:236:\t\t\tplan.Review = reviewPlan(j, rf.Verdict, downgraded, findings)\ninternal/closeout/prepare.go:414:\t\treturn nil, \"\", \"secret scan flagged it (rules: \" + ruleList(res.Findings) + \")\", nil\ninternal/closeout/review.go:58:// reviewPlan splits the findings of a review by whether their line is one the\ninternal/closeout/review.go:150:\tlist, heading := rp.Other, \"Findings outside the changed lines:\"\ninternal/closeout/review.go:154:\t\theading = \"Findings:\"\ninternal/closeout/review.go:156:\t\theading = \"Findings (line placement unavailable):\"\ninternal/closeout/rolefile.go:40:// MaxFindings bounds the findings of one review; MaxFindingPath bounds a\ninternal/closeout/rolefile.go:43:\tMaxFindings    = 50\ninternal/closeout/rolefile.go:64:\t// Findings are a review's findings, in file order. Only a review may have\ninternal/closeout/rolefile.go:66:\tFindings []Finding\ninternal/closeout/rolefile.go:92:\tif rf.Verdict == VerdictApprove && HasBlocking(rf.Findings) {\ninternal/closeout/rolefile.go:115:\tFindings *[]rawFinding `yaml:\"findings\"`\ninternal/closeout/rolefile.go:187:\tif raw.Findings != nil {\ninternal/closeout/rolefile.go:188:\t\tif rf.Findings, err = findingsOf(*raw.Findings); err != nil {\ninternal/closeout/rolefile.go:221:\tif len(rf.Findings) > 0 && j.Stage != StageReview {\ninternal/closeout/rolefile.go:222:\t\treturn malformed(\"findings are allowed only on